              "China's GDP growth in the second quarter closed at 6.2 percent, the lowest rate in at least 27 years. The Trump administration's trade war was the main reason for China's bleak economic data.",
              "# Is China’s Tanking Economy Actually a Win for the US?\n## China's GDP growth for the second quarter slowed to its lowest point in 27 years.\nPresident Donald Trump’s yearlong trade war with China has served its intended purpose. On Monday, China’s government data showed that the country’s second-quarter gross domestic product (GDP) growth rate had hit a new low of 6.2 percent. It’s still an impressive number by developed world standard (U.S",
